### Rationale & Notes

**Platform choices honoured:** Instagram (carousel + caption), Facebook (link post), Pinterest (tall pin + SEO keyword), Threads (text-forward deep thread), Bluesky (compact repost + CTA).

**Campaign compliance:**
- ✅ No paid product, pricing, or "buy now" language — only waitlist CTA
- ✅ All links resolve to `/coming-soon` (gated site)
- ✅ Evergreen Saturday-stroll positioning (publish window holds 2–7 days, any reader projects onto future trip)
- ✅ No "this weekend" or time-specific framing
- ✅ Educational/shareable angle: "getting lost is the plan" is inherently viral for trip planners
- ✅ Kill list respected: no Chelsea Flower Show, no bank holidays, no paid tiers

**Platform-specific adaptations:**
- **Instagram:** Punchy hook, sensory detail per neighbourhood, one CTA buried in closing. Hashtags moved to first comment.
- **Facebook:** Softer intro, link focus, no hard sell.
- **Pinterest:** Keyword-rich title, 200-char description optimised for search ("aimless walks," "hidden lanes"), image ratio noted.
- **Threads:** Narrative thread format (7 posts), one vivid detail per neighbourhood, conversational close with waitlist CTA.
- **Bluesky:** Compact, shareable thread structure (2 posts), less fragmented than Threads, easier to boost via quote-posts.

**Tone:** Insider, unhurried, anti-agenda. Speaks to the Saturday-morning dreamer and the already-booked traveller equally.